00:27:57,454 --> 00:28:01,796
And so this is all being fed into this create root route function from Tanstack

278
00:28:02,478 --> 00:28:06,368
React Router, which takes in the root component that you render.

279
00:28:06,542 --> 00:28:11,364
And of course, this is what gets rendered in the main TSX through the router provider.

280
00:28:12,238 --> 00:28:15,408
So this root component will always be rendered no matter where you are.

281
00:28:16,942 --> 00:28:20,324
And then thanks to the outlet, that's going to render the actual page we're on.

282
00:28:20,686 --> 00:28:31,136
And so by default, we have a single page, the starting root index.tsx or the home page. And this is exactly where we saw here on the homepage of the app.

283
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:42,416
And the reason why we can see this is because unlike Next.js, Tanstack Router is very declarative in its routes, where the first thing we do is define the route const

